    "Iodine in dairy comes from cattle feed + sanitization residues; iodine in seafood from the marine source; iodine in Himalayan salt is TRACE \u2014 common myth that pink salt is iodine-rich.",
    "Selenium content of plant foods varies wildly by soil; values here assume average US soils.",
    "Lutein+zeaxanthin in eggs are framework-adjacent (modern science), included for transparency but not in 90-essentials baseline."
